From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 17:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] SecurityPkg/RngDxe: Reject unavailable raw algorithm

The AArch64 implementation only adds EFI_RNG_ALGORITHM_RAW to the
advertised algorithm array when GetArmTrngVersion() finds a firmware TRNG
backend.  RngGetRNG(), however, unconditionally calls GenerateEntropy()
whenever a caller explicitly requests RAW.

With BaseArmTrngLibNull this violates the protocol's advertised contract
and reaches functions which deliberately assert because no backend exists.
This is observable when an EFI OS loader asks for RAW entropy even though
GetInfo() did not advertise it.

Only dispatch RAW requests when RAW is present in the available algorithm
array.  Otherwise return EFI_UNSUPPORTED as required for an unavailable
algorithm.

Signed-off-by: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
---
 SecurityPkg/RandomNumberGenerator/RngDxe/ArmRngDxe.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/SecurityPkg/RandomNumberGenerator/RngDxe/ArmRngDxe.c b/SecurityPkg/RandomNumberGenerator/RngDxe/ArmRngDxe.c
index 510fc3f7b7..4be3c65b64 100644
--- a/SecurityPkg/RandomNumberGenerator/RngDxe/ArmRngDxe.c
+++ b/SecurityPkg/RandomNumberGenerator/RngDxe/ArmRngDxe.c
@@ -82,6 +82,7 @@ RngGetRNG (
 {
   EFI_STATUS  Status;
   GUID        RngGuid;
+  UINTN       Index;
 
   if ((This == NULL) || (RNGValueLength == 0) || (RNGValue == NULL)) {
     return EFI_INVALID_PARAMETER;
@@ -104,7 +105,17 @@ RngGetRNG (
 
   // Raw algorithm (Trng)
   if (CompareGuid (RNGAlgorithm, &gEfiRngAlgorithmRaw)) {
-    return GenerateEntropy (RNGValueLength, RNGValue);
+    for (Index = 0; Index < mAvailableAlgoArrayCount; Index++) {
+      if (CompareGuid (
+            &mAvailableAlgoArray[Index],
+            &gEfiRngAlgorithmRaw
+            ))
+      {
+        return GenerateEntropy (RNGValueLength, RNGValue);
+      }
+    }
+
+    return EFI_UNSUPPORTED;
   }
 
   //
